            "rationale": "Clause: \"`habeas setup` MUST configure native nextest settings in `.config/nextest.toml` ... so the coverage workflow ... routes each executed test attempt through the per-process collector\", and \"Those settings MUST use nextest's own configuration format.\" The routing is done by the `[[profile.default.scripts]]` rule (`filter = \"all()\"`, `run-wrapper = \"habeas-coverage\"`). The marked `pair[experimental]` only enables wrapper scripts. The marked `table[scripts.wrapper.habeas-coverage]` only defines the wrapper. Without this rule, an alternative would keep both of those settings but never apply the wrapper to any test attempt. No attempt would reach the collector, so the clause would be violated. Nothing marked reaches this table: it is a sibling top-level table in the same file, not a child of either marked item. `fn[configure]` is the generator and does not cover the file's own content. The reviewer can verify here that the rule selects all tests and names the wrapper defined in `scripts.wrapper.habeas-coverage`. The other roots do not show this."
          }
