      "output": {
        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "The marked tests cover every behavioral obligation in `requirements.test-coverage.setup.configuration`.\n\nI did not read the implementation. I judged the tests against the requirement text only.\n\n- **Location at the workspace root.**\n  - `workspace_member_uses_the_native_config_at_the_workspace_root` configures from a member crate and asserts the path is `<root>/.config/nextest.toml`. It also asserts that nothing is written under the member. When the member is excluded from the workspace, it asserts the member's own `.config` is used.\n  - `explicit_workspace_pointer_places_configuration_at_a_sibling_workspace` asserts the path for a sibling workspace reached through an explicit `workspace =` pointer.\n- **Routing every test attempt through the collector, in nextest's own format.**\n  - `native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence` writes the generated source and parses it as TOML. It runs `check` against it for the `ci`, `default` and `local` profiles. It asserts that the habeas wrapper script is present, for example in `scripts`.\n  - The same test confirms the route holds under profile inheritance. A child profile's collector entry overrides an inherited conflicting one. A conflicting entry ordered before the collector fails. A collector with a narrower filter or platform fails. Corrupting `coverage-process` or `within-wrapper` fails.\n  - `coverage_setup_is_idempotent_and_hook_needs_no_coverage_chapter` runs the real `habeas setup` and asserts that the config contains `coverage-process`.\n- **Repeating setup avoids duplicates.**\n  - `native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence` asserts that `configure` on its own output returns identical content. It does this for both the fresh file and the merged file.\n  - The idempotent integration test asserts the file is byte-identical after a second `habeas setup`.\n- **Preserving unrelated nextest settings.**\n  - `native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence` starts from a config with `experimental = ['setup-scripts']`, `retries = 2` and a `setup = 'prepare'` script. It asserts `experimental` has exactly two entries (both `setup-scripts` and `wrapper-scripts`), `retries` is still 2, and the setup script is kept alongside exactly one collector entry.\n- **Reporting conflicts rather than overwriting.**\n  - `setup_conflicts_name_the_setting_and_preserve_existing_native_configuration` covers six conflict forms. They are a wrong collector command, a wrong override setting, a mistyped `experimental`, a mistyped `scripts`, a mistyped `profile.default.scripts`, and a foreign `run-wrapper` script. For each it asserts the error names the setting and `.config/nextest.toml`, and that the file content is unchanged.\n  - `native_settings_inheritance_and_precedence` also asserts a `conflict` error for a foreign wrapper script.\n  - `setup_reports_a_conflicting_nextest_wrapper_without_writing_project_files` runs the real `habeas setup` binary. It asserts failure, an error naming the file and `scripts.wrapper.habeas-coverage`, and that the conflicting config is unchanged.\n  - The idempotent integration test also checks that a conflicting config is left untouched.\n\nI found no uncovered obligation, so I report no gap."
      }
